{
  "module_under_test": "scratchpad_lookup",
  "functional_correctness_confirmed": true,
  "latency_measurements": [
    {
      "bank_select_bit_value": 0,
      "observed_latency_cycles": 1
    },
    {
      "bank_select_bit_value": 1,
      "observed_latency_cycles": 3
    }
  ],
  "report_format_version": "1.0",
  "leaking_index_bits": [
    7
  ],
  "latency_divergent_paths": [
    "case(index[7]) branch in S_IDLE state that selects state <= S_FAST_WAIT when index[7]=0 versus state <= S_SLOW_WAIT1 when index[7]=1",
    "identical case(index[7]) branch duplicated in S_DONE state for back-to-back lookups (start asserted immediately after previous valid)",
    "S_FAST_WAIT state: single-cycle path that computes data_out <= fast_bank[index_latched[6:0]] and asserts valid <= 1'b1 then transitions to S_DONE, yielding 1-cycle start-to-valid latency for index[7]=0",
    "S_SLOW_WAIT1 -> S_SLOW_WAIT2 -> S_SLOW_WAIT3 chain: three sequential FSM states with no useful work in S_SLOW_WAIT1/S_SLOW_WAIT2 (pure state advance) before S_SLOW_WAIT3 computes data_out <= slow_bank[index_latched[6:0]] and asserts valid <= 1'b1, yielding 3-cycle start-to-valid latency for index[7]=1",
    "localparam state encodings S_FAST_WAIT=3'd1 (fast path, reached directly from S_IDLE) versus S_SLOW_WAIT1=3'd2, S_SLOW_WAIT2=3'd3, S_SLOW_WAIT3=3'd4 (slow path, three states traversed) directly encode the index[7]-dependent cycle-count divergence"
  ],
  "mitigation": {
    "strategy": "constant-latency equalization",
    "description": "Equalize the fast-bank path to take the same number of cycles as the slow-bank path so that start-to-valid latency no longer depends on index[7]. Concretely, replace the single S_FAST_WAIT state with a padded three-state sequence (e.g. S_FAST_WAIT1, S_FAST_WAIT2, S_FAST_WAIT3) mirroring the slow bank's S_SLOW_WAIT1/S_SLOW_WAIT2/S_SLOW_WAIT3 structure: in S_FAST_WAIT1 and S_FAST_WAIT2 simply advance state with no data-dependent behavior (index-independent, identical to the slow bank's dummy wait states), and only in the final state (S_FAST_WAIT3) perform data_out <= fast_bank[index_latched[6:0]] and assert valid <= 1'b1, then transition to S_DONE. Both the fast-bank and slow-bank paths then take exactly 3 cycles from start to valid regardless of index[7], removing the timing distinguisher while leaving data_out's value computation (fast_bank[i]=i*3+1, slow_bank[i]=i*5+2 per the offset index_latched[6:0]) completely unchanged, so functional correctness of data_out for both banks is fully preserved. This fix must be applied uniformly to both the S_IDLE-triggered start and the back-to-back S_DONE-triggered start so no residual index[7]-dependent latency remains in either entry path."
  }
}
